    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0192" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d147-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tunis</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-20">20 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From the President to Ambassador Steinhardt.</p>
                <p>Please tell President Inonu I have landed
                    safely in North Africa <pb facs="0193" n="101" xml:id="pg101"/> and that I would
                    greatly welcome him. I cannot make my plans until Monday morning<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d147-f2"/> but will advise you at that time.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d147-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d147-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d147-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the White House, apparently via military channels; forwarded to the
                    Department of State; and forwarded further by the Department, in telegram 904,
                    November 20, 1943, 7 p.m., to the Legation at Ankara, marked “Secret” and “U. S.
                    Urgent”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f2" n="2" xml:id="d147-f2-content">
                <p>November 22, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f3" n="3" xml:id="d147-f3-content">
                <p>For Roosevelt’s next message to Steinhardt, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg386">p. 386</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
